      "short_name": "Old Mysuru",
      "definition": "The former core of the princely Mysore State: Bengaluru Urban and Bengaluru Rural (the IT/BT metro and its industrial periphery), Ramanagara, Mandya, Mysuru and Chamarajanagara (the Vokkaliga-heartland, Cauvery-basin agrarian belt anchored by Mysuru city). Grouped together as the region long governed from and centred on Mysuru/Bengaluru, sharing Old Mysuru Kannada, Vokkaliga social weight and Cauvery-dependent irrigation, distinct from the drier plains to its north-east.",
