      "short_name": "Bayaluseeme",
      "definition": "Kannada 'bayalu seeme' (open country): the semi-arid, rain-shadow central and eastern plains -- Chikkaballapur, Kolar, Tumakuru, Davanagere and Chitradurga. Grouped together as borewell-dependent dryland-farming districts squeezed between the wetter Malnad/Karavali west and the Deccan north, sharing groundwater depletion, drought exposure and heavy out-migration to Bengaluru, distinct from both the Bengaluru metro belt and the Krishna-basin north.",
